      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The biggest difference between the NVIDIA and AMD implementations is the MCTP message type. AMD uses 0x7F (Vendor Defined - IANA), while NVIDIA uses 0x7E, resulting in a different message format.\n\nRight, so make that an argument, and reuse the rest of the code?\n\n\u003e \n\u003e Regarding the MCTP transport layer, we discussed this with @patrick@stwcx.xyz and @pmb@meta.com earlier [1]. We plan to implement the MCTP request/response layer using sdbusplus::async [2] instead of the Boost-based library. The nvidia-gpusensor implementation can migrate to the new library once it is available.\n\u003e \n\u003e [1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/94550/comment/10c40fe3_baa69d09/\n\u003e [2] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/95106\n\nThat\u0027s great;  I don\u0027t think \"I want to use stdexec\" justifies duplicating code.  If we need to make the code work with both executors, lets do that.",
      "parentUuid": "fc16af91_9c6a09c6",
