      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T02:51:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Right, so make that an argument, and reuse the rest of the code?\n\nYes, we have implemented the MCTP transport API that allow caller to define their message format [1].\n\n\u003e That\u0027s great;  I don\u0027t think \"I want to use stdexec\" justifies duplicating code.  If we need to make the code work with both executors, lets do that.\n\nAgreed. The MCTP requester accepts a VdmBinding, so callers can specify their message type, header size, and instance-ID offset. AMD uses 0x7F; nvdia-gpusensor could reuse the same transport with a 0x7E binding. The protocol-specific message encoding and decoding can remain separate.\n\n[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/95106/2/src/MctpAsyncRequester.cpp#69:~:text\u003d69-,VdmBinding%20binding%2C,-70",
      "parentUuid": "782e1b40_102babf3",
